  "kind": "engine.scenario",
  "name": "capture-reuse-decisions",
  "description": "How a reusable (not forced) capture resolves, in Dart's order. The engine offers the dHash baseline of the last accepted (or exactly reused) frame together with that frame's visible structure; the host reports a perceptual match as captured with the baseline's dHash. With the same structure that is perceptual_hash_coalesced: the frame is released and the latest frame reused, and the baseline stays the referenced frame's. Under another structure the frame is new (fresh_accepted). A frame whose content hash equals a compatible retained frame is exact_content_reused: released, that frame reused, and its dHash and structure become the baseline. paintUnchanged reuses the latest compatible frame (paint_generation_unchanged). Forced captures (here a swipe's) get no baseline.",
  "contract": {
    "sessionSchemaVersion": 10,
    "fingerprintSchemaVersion": 6
  },
